// from the motion axis, the rest-frame angle the light actually came from is
//
//     cos psi0 = (cos psi' - beta) / (1 - beta cos psi')
//
// so each pixel de-aberrates its viewing direction and samples the rest-frame sky
// there. The same motion blueshifts and beams the forward sky (Doppler factor
// delta = 1/(gamma(1 - beta cos psi')) > 1 ahead) and redshifts/dims the rear.
// beta oscillates from ~0 to ~0.95. Verified on-device: forward and rear are fixed
// points, psi'=90deg maps to rest 120deg at beta=0.5, forward/rear Doppler are
// sqrt((1+-beta)/(1-+beta)), and the small-beta limit reproduces Bradley's 20.5"
// constant of stellar aberration.

